<header class="about-hero"><div class="shell about-hero-grid"><div><h1>Why I closed the agency.</h1><p class="page-lede">I founded Upstack Studio in 2017. Years later, I chose to shut it down. Here’s what I took from that chapter, and what I’m building now.</p><nav class="page-jumps" aria-label="My story"><a href="#agency-years">The agency years</a><a href="#the-decision">The decision</a><a href="#what-im-building">What’s next</a></nav></div><figure><img src="/assets/images/adrian/adrian-in-conversation.webp" data-mobile-crop="4/3" data-mobile-position="38" alt="Adrian Ching in conversation across a table at a café" width="1600" height="1664" fetchpriority="high"></figure></div></header>
<section class="section" id="agency-years"><div class="shell agency-chapter"><div><h2>It started with building for other people.</h2><p>I founded Upstack Studio in 2017. For years, my team and I built web and mobile software with business owners.</p><p>The job went beyond getting an app to work. We had to understand customers, choose which features to build and make the project worth the cost.</p><p>That’s where I learned to look past the feature list. The hard part was rarely just the code.</p></div><figure class="team-photo"><img src="/assets/images/adrian/dinner-group.webp" alt="Adrian Ching at dinner with a group" width="1600" height="1200" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><figcaption>A conversation over dinner.</figcaption></figure></div></section>
<section class="section section-soft"><div class="shell agency-chapter tradelink-story"><div><h2>A working product is only part of the answer.</h2><p>Take Tradelink. My team and I built the first version of its transport management software to replace an earlier no-code product.</p><p>The work brought loads, trips and trailers into one product. We had to work out what the business needed its software to handle next.</p><p>With each new idea, I ask how it would help the person using it.</p><a class="text-link" href="/client-stories/">Hear from the people we built with{{ icon("arrow", "link-arrow") }}</a></div><figure><img src="/assets/images/work/tradelink.jpg" alt="Tradelink software screens for managing transport loads, trips and trailers" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><figcaption>Tradelink · Built with the Upstack Studio team.</figcaption></figure></div></section>
<section class="section decision-chapter" id="the-decision"><div class="reading"><h2>I could keep doing it.<br>That wasn’t enough.</h2><p>I could have kept improving the model. But it was no longer the company I wanted to build. I wanted to own the products, own the results and focus on fewer, bigger ideas.</p><p>If you’ve built a business, you may know how hard it is to separate “I can keep doing this” from “I should keep doing this.”</p><p class="story-turn">I shut the agency down to focus on products and businesses I own.</p><p>AI has opened up more possibilities for what comes next. I’m interested in what a small team can do when AI handles repeatable work and people keep judgment, relationships and the important decisions.</p></div></section>
<section class="section section-soft" id="what-im-building"><div class="shell current-work"><h2>What I’m building now.</h2><div class="current-company"><h3 class="icon-heading">{{ icon("building", "") }}Second Team</h3><p>Second Team gets most of my time. I’m building it for the long term.</p><p>I share the lessons from building while keeping the product work private.</p></div><div class="current-company"><h3 class="icon-heading">{{ icon("portfolio", "") }}My portfolio</h3><p>Alongside Second Team, I’m building software, media and other businesses I own and operate.</p><p>This website is the home for that work, my writing, videos and future products.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="shell values-grid"><h2>A few rules I come back to.</h2><div class="values-list"><p>Understand the business problem before choosing a tool.</p><p>Tell the truth, even when the answer is “do not build it.”</p><p>Do fewer things and give them proper attention.</p><p>Let AI handle repeatable work. Keep people on judgment and relationships.</p></div></div></section>
